    "faq.a0":
      "Your feed stays in an isolated session attached to your browser. Nothing is shared, nothing leaves the server beyond the API calls required to parse and query it. Sessions are wiped automatically after 1 hour of inactivity.",
    "faq.q1": "Will read mode stay free?",
    "faq.a1":
      "Yes. Read mode is free forever, with no signup and no usage limits worth thinking about.",
    "faq.q2": "How do I get edit access?",
    "faq.a2":
      "The edit mode is in private beta. Use the secondary button in the hero to send us a quick email with your organization and what you need to fix. We send a code back if you are a transit team that ships GTFS feeds.",
    "faq.q3": "Can I self-host GTFS Express?",
    "faq.a3":
      "Yes. The whole stack is Docker-based, runs on a 2 GB VPS, and takes one command to deploy. Your data stays on your hardware.",
    "faq.q4": "What about GTFS-Realtime?",
    "faq.a4":
      "Not supported today. We focus on GTFS Schedule. Realtime support is on the roadmap.",
    "faq.q5": "Why are there two modes?",
    "faq.a5":
      "Read mode serves anyone who needs to inspect a feed: analysts, journalists, integrators, agencies. Edit mode is heavier (it lets you mass-update and re-publish data), so it stays gated until we are confident the workflow is bulletproof on every kind of feed.",

    "mailto.subject": "GTFS Express edit access request",
    "mailto.body":
      "Hello,\n\nI'd like to request access to GTFS Express's edit mode (private beta).\n\nOrganization:\nCountry / region:\nWhat I want to fix or republish:\n\nThanks!",

